        {
          "passage_id": "P2",
          "quote": "Year ending Mar. 2021 | 1,200,000 | (8.3) | 300,000 | (14.9) | 290,000 | 200,000(19.5)(22.7) | 1,678.93"
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "P3",
          "quote": "profit attributable to owners of parent of 200.0 billion yen."
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "P2",
          "quote": "(Reference) Non-consolidated Results"
        }
      ],
      "calculation_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Nintendo reported COVID-19-related production and shipment delays for Switch consoles, Joy-Con controllers and Ring Fit Adventure in some regions in February and March, with limited impact on FY2020 results (PDF p. 3). The disclosure does not identify a specific component shortage. For FY2021, the risk is that persistent shortages of parts constrain console assembly, limiting both hardware sales and the number of new owners buying games.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "passage_id": "P4",
          "quote": "Because of COVID-19, production and shipments of the Nintendo Switch console, accessories like the Joy-Con controllers, and Ring\nFit Adventure faced delays in some regions from February through March"
