        {
          "passage_id": "P4",
          "quote": "this only had limited impact on business results for this\nfiscal year."
        }
      ],
      "calculation_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "analysis": {
    "text": "Base case as of May 8, 2020: higher than guidance for the year ending March 31, 2021. The main driver is software sales to existing Switch owners: Animal Crossing’s record start gives Nintendo a way to outperform even if near-term hardware shipments are constrained (PDF pp. 3–4). Under the stated rule, ‘higher’ means above ¥200,000 million × (1 + 0.02); ‘within’ runs from ¥200,000 million × (1 − 0.02) through that upper threshold, inclusive.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "passage_id": "P4",
        "quote": "Animal Crossing: New Horizons, released in March, sold 11.77 million units, which is now the best start ever\nfor a Nintendo Switch title."
      },
      {
        "passage_id": "P3",
        "quote": "the\ncombination of existing popular titles and a continuous stream of appealing new titles will work together to invigorate the platform."
