  },
  "alternative_and_signal": {
    "text": "Downside alternative: profit finishes below the lower edge of the band if prolonged component shortages cut console shipments enough that software sales to existing owners cannot make up for lost hardware sales and game purchases by new owners. I would switch to ‘lower’ if Nintendo materially cuts its full-year Switch unit forecast and attributes the cut to continuing component shortages rather than a temporary shipping delay (PDF pp. 3–4).",
    "citations": [
      {
        "passage_id": "P4",
        "quote": "Fit Adventure faced delays in some regions from February through March"
      },
      {
        "passage_id": "P3",
